      <workList xml:id="workDesc_cd5db651">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e219216">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_451cfdbd">A4:500</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_e3313901" xml:lang="it">I Quadro à 2 violini, oboe e basso</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_69857a9e">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_99adc33a">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_e52af363">
               <p xml:id="idm78">The present ‘Quadro’, which is listed in the Breitkopf catalogues of 1761 and 1763 as part of a collection including works by <persName xml:id="idm79" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Christian Gottfried Krause</persName>, <persName xml:id="idm80" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Johann Adolph Hasse</persName>, <persName xml:id="idm81" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Georg Philipp Telemann</persName>, and a <persName xml:id="idm82" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Rosetti</persName>, seems to have been lost. In the catalogue of 1763, which includes incipits, it is evident that the work is identical to SchW A4:501 for flauto obligato and strings. It is likely that the work was composed before Scheibe’s arrival in Copenhagen in 1740. In 1836, it was auctioned by Breitkopf.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_dcf9bfd0">
               <language xml:id="da">Danish</language>
               <language xml:id="it">Italian</language>
               <language xml:id="en">English</language>
            </langUsage>
